# Private documents — never publish
*.docx
*.pdf
*.odt
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.pptx
# Office lock files, which are created beside any open document
~$*

# ...except the three engagement sheets, which are published downloads on the site.
# *.pdf above would otherwise silently keep them out of the repo and 404 the links.
# One negation per file: a pattern like !assets/*.pdf would publish anything dropped
# into assets/, which is how a private document reaches a public repo by accident.
!assets/delivery-readiness-review.pdf
!assets/assessment-and-workable-response.pdf
!assets/assessment-through-implementation.pdf

# Local workspace
.claude/
.netlify/

# Session briefing for Claude Code. Deliberately NOT committed: Netlify serves the
# repo root, so a committed CLAUDE.md would be public at alefurtado.org/CLAUDE.md.
CLAUDE.md

# Personal working files — not for the public repo
linkedin/
video/
Videos/

# Strategy working docs — Drive only, never in the repo
Website handovers/
Website direction plan.html

# Analytics exports. Ignored by name, not by extension: the folder held only a PDF,
# so `*.pdf` above happened to cover it, and a CSV or PNG dropped in there would have
# been published at the repo root on the next `git add -A`.
Cloudfare reports/

